{
  "entityR1": {
    "feedback": "Written before this candidate races, so no outcome is stated for it. The candidate is valid. Its five sensors sit at x = -0.02 to +0.02 in 0.01 m steps, y = 0.03, inside the allowed ranges. Weights are antisymmetric in [-2, 2], and kp, ki, kd, base_speed, mass and line_loss are in range. Nothing is obviously broken.\n\nThe change is relative to iteration 6 (best raced, 115.8). Iterations 0 to 6 all ended off_track on every trial, with max_error at 0.061 to 0.064 and 1 to 2 line-loss events per run. The evidence points to a line-loss problem at bends, not jitter: steering_oscillation has stayed at 0.07 to 0.28, and kd 0.45 in iteration 6 raised it. Four things change at once: sensor_size goes from 8 mm to 12 mm, kd from 0.45 to 0.35, mass from 0.7 to 0.6 kg, and base_speed from 1.2 back to 1.3. The race will not isolate which one matters.\n\nTwo risks. First, 12 mm footprints at 10 mm spacing overlap heavily, so the signal may be blurred. Iteration 0 used 12 mm and scored lowest, though with different gains, so that result cannot be read as a clean footprint effect. Second, base_speed 1.3 is the iteration 4 value, and iteration 4 reached 0.44 on oval, so progress should hold if the line is kept.\n\nI am approving because the design is valid, it is a sensible step from the best raced design, and this is still early enough in the run (4 iterations after this one) that a race is worth more than a revision made on numbers alone. The next critique should follow the race. If line_loss_events fall to 1 or fewer and max_error stays at or above 0.06, raise kp before adding kd, as iterations 4 and 6 suggest. If the footprint change blurs the signal (progress falls below iteration 6 on oval while the line is held), return sensor_size to 0.008 and keep the new kd and mass. If steering_oscillation rises above about 0.3, reduce kd toward 0.3.",
    "requested_changes": [
      "If line_loss_events are 1 or fewer but max_error stays at or above 0.06, raise kp from 3.0 toward 3.5 with the sensors and kd held, because iterations 0 to 6 show line loss at bends rather than oscillation (steering_oscillation about 0.1 to 0.28).",
      "If progress on oval falls below iteration 6's 0.49 while the line is held, return sensor_size to 0.008 (the iteration 6 value), keeping the 0.01 m spacing, since iteration 0's 12 mm result was confounded and the blur may be the cause.",
      "If steering_oscillation rises above about 0.3 with kd 0.35, lower kd toward 0.3 rather than raising it, since iteration 6 showed kd 0.45 pushing steering_oscillation to 0.28 on oval."
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entityR1": {
      "label": "Approve: 12mm sensing test",
      "notes": "Approved the 12 mm footprint, kd 0.35, mass 0.6 and base 1.3 design as a valid step from the best raced design (iteration 6, 115.8). Multiple changes are confounded, so the race will show which change matters and the next feedback names the fallback for each."
    }
  }
}
